WEBVTT
Language: en

00:00:00.537 --> 00:00:02.525
A Moroccan sultan's Qur'an,

00:00:02.525 --> 00:00:03.750
in his own hand,

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:05.462
at the al-Aqsa Mosque.

00:00:05.512 --> 00:00:08.537
Another, from the royal
library of al-Mansur,

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:09.475
in Spain.

00:00:09.525 --> 00:00:10.337
And a third,

00:00:10.337 --> 00:00:11.200
in Munich.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.112
Morocco's Qur'an manuscripts are

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.913
scattered across the world.

00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:17.300
Now, one guide brings them together:

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.175
Masahif al-Maghrib.

00:00:19.675 --> 00:00:20.813
Twelve centuries,

00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:22.025
seven dynasties,

00:00:22.025 --> 00:00:24.150
and more than sixty Qur'ans:

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:25.475
those that survive,

00:00:25.475 --> 00:00:27.151
and those that were lost.

00:00:27.201 --> 00:00:29.088
Some were copied by a caliph or

00:00:29.088 --> 00:00:30.988
a sultan in his own hand;

00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:33.463
others written in gold on lapis blue,

00:00:33.463 --> 00:00:35.476
or in silver on green paper.

00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:36.563
Each one has a card

00:00:36.563 --> 00:00:37.888
that tells its story,

00:00:37.888 --> 00:00:39.901
with close-up samples of the script,

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.213
and links to the digitized copies.

00:00:42.263 --> 00:00:44.888
Prepared by Ibrahim Hassani Idrissi,

00:00:44.888 --> 00:00:48.026
a calligrapher and manuscript
researcher from Fez,

00:00:48.026 --> 00:00:49.976
who teaches Maghribi scripts,

00:00:49.976 --> 00:00:52.150
holds a Diploma in the Art of Calligraphy

00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:53.413
from al-Qarawiyyin,

00:00:53.413 --> 00:00:55.076
and won the Encouragement Prize of the

00:00:55.076 --> 00:00:58.276
Mohammed VI Award for
Maghribi Calligraphy.

00:00:58.326 --> 00:00:59.788
A well-sourced guide,

00:00:59.788 --> 00:01:01.451
in Arabic and English,

00:01:01.451 --> 00:01:02.888
for every researcher,

00:01:02.888 --> 00:01:06.226
calligrapher, and lover
of Morocco's heritage.

00:01:06.276 --> 00:01:09.213
Visit masahif-al-maghrib.com
